/-! # Localization for equivariant coherent Grothendieck groups

Source: agent-formulated supporting lemma for Milne, Algebraic Groups, Section 22d,
Theorem 22.50, p.480. The proof assembles Stacks 09VH, 077S, 01Y9 and 087T;
Milne does not itself state this localization lemma.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-equivariant-coherent-localization-sequence)

The groups, linearizations, rational representations and operation predicates are the
shared constructions. In particular `IsPushforward` specifies ordinary closed direct
image through its equivariant counit, rather than a higher-image Euler characteristic.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option relaxedAutoImplicit false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.EquivariantCoherent

/-- Restriction and ordinary closed pushforward give the integral R(G)-linear
localization sequence, without a regularity or reducedness hypothesis.
Source: agent-formulated supporting lemma for Milne, Algebraic Groups, Section 22d,
Theorem 22.50, p.480; Stacks 09VH, 077S, 01Y9 and 087T.
(blueprint: lem-sfb-equivariant-coherent-localization-sequence).

Proof:
1. Use the action groupoid with object scheme $Y$, arrow scheme $G\times_FY$, target $a$ and
source $\operatorname{pr}_2$. Its two projections are affine and flat:
$G\to\operatorname{Spec}F$ is flat by [lem-pc-flat-field], affine by hypothesis, and
$\operatorname{pr}_2$ is its base change; the automorphism $(g,y)\mapsto(g,gy)$ identifies $a$
with $\operatorname{pr}_2$. Explicitly on affine charts flatness is exactness of
$-\otimes_FF[G]$, and localizations preserve that exactness. Affine maps are quasi-compact and
quasi-separated by [lem-weil-pbc-affine-morphism-permanence]. Both groupoid schemes, and
$Y,W,U$, are Noetherian by [lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-over-noetherian], since a field is
Noetherian; every open of a Noetherian scheme is quasi-compact. Invariance makes the open and
closed action-groupoid morphisms Cartesian on source and target. Therefore
[lem-sfb-cartesian-groupoid-pushforward-adjunction] applies to $j$ and $i$: their ordinary
quasi-coherent direct images have equivariant structures and equivariant adjunction units. By
[lem-sfb-groupoid-module-limits-colimits] and [lem-weil-pbc-coherent-kernel-cokernel-locnoeth],
equivariant coherent modules have the underlying kernels, images, cokernels and finite sums.
Restriction is exact, as its stalk maps are identities. Closed direct image is exact as its
stalks are the original stalks on $W$ and zero off $W$; its coherence and identification with
the stipulated group map are also [lem-sfb-equivariant-coherent-proper-pushforward].
2. For a coherent equivariant module $N$ on $U$, apply
[lem-sfb-equivariant-coherent-submodule-extension] to $M=j_*N$ and the identity submodule
$N=j^*j_*N$. The direct image is quasi-coherent and equivariant by step 1; $j^*j_*N=N$ follows
by evaluating on opens contained in $U$. We obtain a coherent equivariant extension $E\subseteq
j_*N$. Thus every generator of $G_0^G(U)$ lifts. Let $H\subseteq G_0^G(Y)$ be the subgroup
generated by all $[K]$ with $j^*K=0$, and put $Q=G_0^G(Y)/H$. Restriction vanishes on $H$, so
induces $\bar j:Q\to G_0^G(U)$.
3. The class in $Q$ of an extension does not depend on the extension or the chosen
identification on $U$. Indeed, given extensions $E,E'$ and an equivariant isomorphism
$h:j^*E\simeq j^*E'$, extend its graph, a coherent equivariant submodule of $j^*(E\oplus E')$,
to $L\subseteq E\oplus E'$ by [lem-sfb-equivariant-coherent-submodule-extension]. Each
projection $p:L\to E$ or $E'$ restricts to an isomorphism. Its kernel and cokernel are coherent
equivariant modules supported on $W$ by step 1. The two short exact sequences through
$\operatorname{im}p$ give $[L]-[E]=[\ker p]-[\operatorname{coker}p]\in H$ and the same formula
for $E'$. Hence $[E]=[E']$ in $Q$.
4. The assignment $[N]\mapsto[E]\bmod H$ respects every defining short exact relation on $U$.
For $0\to N'\to N\to N''\to0$, choose any extension $E$ of $N$ from step 2. Extend the submodule
$N'\subseteq j^*E$ to $E'\subseteq E$ by [lem-sfb-equivariant-coherent-submodule-extension].
Then $E/E'$ is coherent equivariant and restricts to $N''$ by step 1, so $[E]=[E']+[E/E']$.
Independence from step 3 proves the required relation for any choices of extensions. We obtain a
homomorphism $b:G_0^G(U)\to Q$. It is inverse to $\bar j$: restriction of an extension is its
original module, and every coherent equivariant module on $Y$ is itself an extension of its
restriction. Thus $\ker j^*=H$.
5. Let $I$ be the ideal of $W$. For every generator $[K]$ of $H$, its support lies in $|W|$, so
[lem-weil-pbc-coherent-support-power-ideal-kills] gives $I^nK=0$ for some $n\geq0$. The ideal
$I$ is equivariant: it is the kernel of the equivariant map $\mathcal O_Y\to i_*\mathcal O_W$ of
step 1. Its powers and the submodules $I^rK$ are preserved by linearization, since the two flat
pullbacks preserve images of multiplication. These images are quasi-coherent by
[lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-tensor-product-affine-sections] and
[lem-weil-pbc-quasi-coherent-module-cokernel-image], and coherent as submodules of $K$ by
[lem-weil-pbc-coherent-kernel-cokernel-locnoeth]. The finite filtration has coherent equivariant
quotients $Q_r=I^rK/I^{r+1}K$ annihilated by $I$.
6. By [lem-weil-pbc-closed-immersion-coherent-equivalence] (1), write $Q_r\simeq i_*A_r$ with
$A_r$ coherent on $W$. The linearization descends: pull back along $a$ and
$\operatorname{pr}_2$, use their Cartesian squares with $i$ and the degree-zero isomorphisms of
[lem-pc-flat-base-change-cohom] to view the linearization of $Q_r$ as an isomorphism between
closed direct images on $G\times_FY$. Full faithfulness of the same closed-immersion equivalence
gives a unique isomorphism on $G\times_FW$. Its identity and cocycle equations follow by
faithfulness after direct image on $W$ and $G\times_FG\times_FW$, respectively. Thus $A_r$ is
equivariant. The filtration relations give $[K]=\sum_{r=0}^{n-1}[Q_r]=i_*\sum_r[A_r]$; if $n=0$,
$K=0$ and the sum is empty. Hence $H\subseteq\operatorname{im}i_*$. Conversely $j^*i_*A=0$ on
every open in $U$, so $\operatorname{im}i_*\subseteq H$. Together with steps 2 and 4 this proves
exactness, without replacing $W$ by its reduction.
7. Finally $j^*(M\otimes_FV)=(j^*M)\otimes_FV$ for every finite-dimensional rational $G$-module
$V$. Also $i_*(A\otimes_FV)\simeq(i_*A)\otimes_FV$: in a basis of $V$ both sides are the same
finite sum of the underlying sheaf, and the basis-free map on sections $a\otimes v\mapsto
a\otimes v$ commutes with the diagonal linearizations. Tensoring with $V$ is exact since it is a
finite sum locally, and similarly exact sequences of $F$-representations remain exact after
tensoring a sheaf (they split as $F$-vector spaces). Thus both maps commute with the actions of
representation generators and hence with $R(G)$. If $W=\varnothing$, $I=\mathcal O_Y$ and the
only supported coherent module is zero; if $U=\varnothing$, every coherent module is covered by
the same finite filtration argument. The construction also permits $Y=\varnothing$, nonreduced
$W$, and nonsmooth $G$.
The symbols i_* and j^* in these steps are exactly the ordinary equivariant
adjunction predicate `IsPushforward` and the normalized `IsPullback`. Their underlying
module pullback, counit and composition comparisons are the shared constructions.
-/
theorem equivariant_coherent_localization_sequence
    (F : Type u) [Field F] (G Y W U : Over (Spec (.of F)))
    [GrpObj G] [ModObj G Y] [ModObj G W] [ModObj G U]
    [IsAffine G.left] [LocallyOfFiniteType G.hom] [QuasiCompact G.hom]
    [IsSeparated Y.hom] [LocallyOfFiniteType Y.hom] [QuasiCompact Y.hom]
    (i : W ⟶ Y) [IsModHom G i] [IsClosedImmersion i.left]
    (j : U ⟶ Y) [IsModHom G j] [IsOpenImmersion j.left]
    (hU : Set.range j.left = (Set.range i.left)ᶜ) :
    ∃ (DY : ActionGroupoidModel G Y) (DW : ActionGroupoidModel G W)
      (DU : ActionGroupoidModel G U)
      (r : CommRing (RepresentationGZero F Γ(G.left, ⊤)))
      (mY : @Module (RepresentationGZero F Γ(G.left, ⊤)) (GZero DY)
        r.toSemiring inferInstance)
      (mW : @Module (RepresentationGZero F Γ(G.left, ⊤)) (GZero DW)
        r.toSemiring inferInstance)
      (mU : @Module (RepresentationGZero F Γ(G.left, ⊤)) (GZero DU)
        r.toSemiring inferInstance),
      IsRepresentationRing r ∧ IsRepresentationAction F DY r mY ∧
        IsRepresentationAction F DW r mW ∧ IsRepresentationAction F DU r mU ∧
      ∃ (push : GZero DW →+ GZero DY) (restrict : GZero DY →+ GZero DU),
        (∀ N : Coherent DW, ∃ M : Coherent DY, IsPushforward i N M) ∧
        (∀ (N : Coherent DW) (M : Coherent DY), IsPushforward i N M →
          push (classOf N) = classOf M) ∧
        (∀ M : Coherent DY, ∃ N : Coherent DU, IsPullback j M N) ∧
        (∀ (M : Coherent DY) (N : Coherent DU), IsPullback j M N →
          restrict (classOf M) = classOf N) ∧
        (∀ (a : RepresentationGZero F Γ(G.left, ⊤)) (z : GZero DW),
          push (mW.smul a z) = mY.smul a (push z)) ∧
        (∀ (a : RepresentationGZero F Γ(G.left, ⊤)) (z : GZero DY),
          restrict (mY.smul a z) = mU.smul a (restrict z)) ∧
        Function.Surjective restrict ∧ AddMonoidHom.range push = AddMonoidHom.ker restrict := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.EquivariantCoherent
